   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">One sidenote: </span></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Originally, I have three potential moderators in my data - </span><span style=\"font-family:Segoe,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">In order to test the unique contribution of PS as a moderator, I wanted to compare the main model of interest with two other models including each potential moderator </span><span style=\"font-family:Segoe,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">using the model chi square, the CFI and RMSEA to evaluate goodness-of-fit. Now it does not look like a good idea..... I am wondering if I just  need to compare estimates and SE with one another.</span></div><br></div>"
