  {
   "id": "rEz6uFi0AAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2020-08-27T15:05:59Z",
   "subject": "Re: model fit with a moderator",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">riskc&lt;-scale(semdata$risk,center=TRUE,scale=FALSE)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">semdata$PSc&lt;-scale(SUMMER_final$PS,center = TRUE,scale = FALSE)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">xz&lt;-riskc*PSc</span></p><p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">mod1&lt;-lm(MH~ riskc+PSc+xz+gender+age)</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This came up in an earlier thread, where I explained that you need to be consistent in where you store your new variables.  If you use the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>argument to tell<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lm() </font>where to find variables, then each variable should be in that<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>set.  The syntax above does not provide a<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>argument to<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lm()</font>, so although it can find the objects riskc and xz, it would not find PSc, which is stored in semdata.  However, you calculated xz from an object called PSc, so clearly you created that stand-alone object outside the syntax you shared.</div><div><br></div><div>Regardless...</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">summary(mod1, fit.measures=TRUE)</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mod1</font> is an <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">lm</font> object, not a <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">lavaan</font> object.</div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:Segoe,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">In order to test the unique contribution of PS as a moderator, I wanted to compare the main model of interest with two other models including each potential moderator </span><span style=\"font-family:Segoe,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">using the model chi square, the CFI and RMSEA to evaluate goodness-of-fit. </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>In order for models to be comparable, they need to be fit to the same variables (including interaction terms).  So you would need to include all moderators in each model, and take turns fixing effects of different moderators to zero.  Then models can be compared, but only using fit measures that do not require nesting, such as information criteria (e.g., AIC, BIC) and incremental fit indices (e.g., CFI, TLI).</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420835791000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1SUAC7hffhVmJXmDFZM5G-\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
